#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:59
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:61
msgid "`regenerate(value1, value2, value3, ...)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:63
msgid ""
"The main Regenerate function. Calling this function creates a new set "
"that gets a chainable API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:78
msgid ""
"Any arguments passed to `regenerate()` will be added to the set right "
"away. Both code points (numbers) and symbols (strings consisting of a "
"single Unicode symbol) are accepted, as well as arrays containing values "
"of these types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:89
msgid "`regenerate.prototype.add(value1, value2, value3, ...)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:91
msgid ""
"Any arguments passed to `add()` are added to the set. Both code points "
"(numbers) and symbols (strings consisting of a single Unicode symbol) are"
" accepted, as well as arrays containing values of these types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:102
msgid ""
"It’s also possible to pass in a Regenerate instance. Doing so adds all "
"code points in that instance to the current set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:110
msgid ""
"Note that the initial call to `regenerate()` acts like `add()`. This "
"allows you to create a new Regenerate instance and add some code points "
"to it in one go:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:117
msgid "`regenerate.prototype.remove(value1, value2, value3, ...)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:119
msgid ""
"Any arguments passed to `remove()` are removed from the set. Both code "
"points (numbers) and symbols (strings consisting of a single Unicode "
"symbol) are accepted, as well as arrays containing values of these types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:126
msgid ""
"It’s also possible to pass in a Regenerate instance. Doing so removes all"
" code points in that instance from the current set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:134
msgid "`regenerate.prototype.addRange(start, end)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:136
msgid ""
"Adds a range of code points from `start` to `end` (inclusive) to the set."
" Both code points (numbers) and symbols (strings consisting of a single "
"Unicode symbol) are accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:146
msgid "`regenerate.prototype.removeRange(start, end)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:148
msgid ""
"Removes a range of code points from `start` to `end` (inclusive) from the"
" set. Both code points (numbers) and symbols (strings consisting of a "
"single Unicode symbol) are accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:164
msgid "`regenerate.prototype.intersection(codePoints)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:166
msgid ""
"Removes any code points from the set that are not present in both the set"
" and the given `codePoints` array. `codePoints` must be an array of "
"numeric code point values, i.e. numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:176
msgid ""
"Instead of the `codePoints` array, it’s also possible to pass in a "
"Regenerate instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:188
msgid "`regenerate.prototype.contains(value)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:190
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if the given value is part of the set, and `false` "
"otherwise. Both code points (numbers) and symbols (strings consisting of "
"a single Unicode symbol) are accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:200
msgid "`regenerate.prototype.clone()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:202
msgid ""
"Returns a clone of the current code point set. Any actions performed on "
"the clone won’t mutate the original set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:213
msgid "`regenerate.prototype.toString(options)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:215
msgid ""
"Returns a string representing (part of) a regular expression that matches"
" all the symbols mapped to the code points within the set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:222
msgid ""
"If the `bmpOnly` property of the optional `options` object is set to "
"`true`, the output matches surrogates individually, regardless of whether"
" they’re lone surrogates or just part of a surrogate pair. This "
"simplifies the output, but it can only be used in case you’re certain the"
" strings it will be used on don’t contain any astral symbols."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:238
msgid ""
"Note that lone low surrogates cannot be matched accurately using regular "
"expressions in JavaScript without the use of [lookbehind "
"assertions](https://mathiasbynens.be/notes/es-regexp-"
"proposals#lookbehinds), which aren't yet widely supported. Regenerate’s "
"output makes a best-effort approach but [there can be false negatives in "
"this "
"regard](https://github.com/mathiasbynens/regenerate/issues/28#issuecomment-72224808)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:240
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If the `hasUnicodeFlag` property of the optional `options` object is set "
"to `true`, the output makes use of Unicode code point escapes (`\\u{…}`) "
"where applicable. This simplifies the output at the cost of compatibility"
" and portability, since it means the output can only be used as a pattern"
" in a regular expression with [the ES6 `u` "
"flag](https://mathiasbynens.be/notes/es6-unicode-regex) enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:252
msgid "`regenerate.prototype.toRegExp(flags = '')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:254
msgid ""
"Returns a regular expression that matches all the symbols mapped to the "
"code points within the set. Optionally, you can pass "
"[flags](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-"
"US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/RegExp#Parameters) to be "
"added to the regular expression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:269
msgid ""
"**Note:** This probably shouldn’t be used. Regenerate is intended as a "
"tool that is used as part of a build process, not at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:271
msgid "`regenerate.prototype.valueOf()` or `regenerate.prototype.toArray()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:273
msgid "Returns a sorted array of unique code points in the set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:283
msgid "`regenerate.version`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:285
msgid "A string representing the semantic version number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:287
msgid "Combine Regenerate with other libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:289
msgid ""
"Regenerate gets even better when combined with other libraries such as "
"[Punycode.js](https://mths.be/punycode). Here’s an example where "
"[Punycode.js](https://mths.be/punycode) is used to convert a string into "
"an array of code points, that is then passed on to Regenerate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:304
msgid ""
"In ES6 you can do something similar with [`Array.from`](https://mths.be"
"/array-from) which uses [the string’s "
"iterator](https://mathiasbynens.be/notes/javascript-unicode#iterating-"
"over-symbols) to split the given string into an array of strings that "
"each contain a single symbol. "
"[`regenerate()`](#regenerateprototypeaddvalue1-value2-value3-) accepts "
"both strings and code points, remember?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:318
msgid "Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:320
msgid ""
"Regenerate supports at least Chrome 27+, Firefox 3+, Safari 4+, Opera "
"10+, IE 6+, Node.js v0.10.0+, io.js v1.0.0+, Narwhal 0.3.2+, RingoJS "
"0.8+, PhantomJS 1.9.0+, and Rhino 1.7RC4+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:322
msgid "Unit tests & code coverage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:324
msgid ""
"After cloning this repository, run `npm install` to install the "
"dependencies needed for Regenerate development and testing. You may want "
"to install Istanbul _globally_ using `npm install istanbul -g`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:326
msgid ""
"Once that’s done, you can run the unit tests in Node using `npm test` or "
"`node tests/tests.js`. To run the tests in Rhino, Ringo, Narwhal, and web"
" browsers as well, use `grunt test`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regenerate_README.md:328
msgid "To generate the code coverage report, use `grunt cover`."
msgstr ""

